# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The image is built with `COPY . .`, so everything tracked in the repo and not
# listed here ends up in the deployed artifact. The entries below are the ones
# that must never ship. This file is a blocklist by nature, so when something
# new is added to the repo, ask whether it belongs in production before it
# becomes part of the image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A second, unrelated Laravel application living inside this repository
# (it requires PHP ^8.3 / laravel/framework ^13 — this app runs PHP 8.2 /
# Laravel 12). Nothing serves it, nothing tests it, and nothing patches it,
# yet `COPY . .` would ship its whole source tree — and its dependency
# manifests — inside our production image.
TaskFlow/

# Working notes / session memory. Internal, and not part of the application.
.workbuddy-ai/

# Postman collections and environment files carry dev credentials
# (`learner_password`, seeded tokens) and the live base_url. They are fixtures
# for manual testing, never runtime config. `*postman*` (not `postman_*`) so it
# also catches `SkillSpan_API_Collection.postman_collection.json`.
*postman*.json

# Handoff / review / incident reports. Documentation for humans, not assets.
# `**/` because a bare `*.md` only matches at the context root.
**/*.md
**/*.pdf
**/*.patch

# Standalone HTML handoff / preview documents (EVIDENCE_ADD_API.html,
# FRONTEND_API_HANDOFF.html, PREVIEW_admin_profile.html). Root-anchored with a
# leading `/` on purpose: the only runtime HTML is Blade (`.blade.php`), so this
# must never reach into `public/` or `resources/`.
/*.html
